<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-08-25T12:17:10+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Tue, 25 Aug 2026 12:17:10 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists turn plastic waste into protein cookies; food can tackle hunger and feed space crews]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133452916.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Researchers at Southern Illinois University Carbondale are developing protein-rich cookies made using plastic waste and agricultural waste. Called µBites, the cookies use PET plastic from bottles and discarded corn stalks and leaves. Programmed yeasts convert processed waste into proteins, fats, acids and flavouring molecules. The NASA-linked project is aimed at developing food for resource-limited environments, including future deep-space missions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-turned-plastic-bottles-and-corn-waste-into-protein-rich-cookies-the-food-could-help-tackle-hunger-problem-and-also-feed-space-crews/articleshow/133452916.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-turned-plastic-bottles-and-corn-waste-into-protein-rich-cookies-the-food-could-help-tackle-hunger-problem-and-also-feed-space-crews/articleshow/133452916.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T12:00:16+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133497076,imgsize-92171.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[“I deceived people, I lied”: Woman pretended to be a child for years, convicted of fraud]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133496640.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a shocking case from Brazil, Amanda Maria Souza de Oliveira was found guilty of fraud and assuming a false identity, having lived undetected as a child for years. Although she confessed to her masquerade, she maintained that her motivations were rooted in personal vulnerability rather than dishonesty. The court, however, sentenced her to prison for her deceptive actions, highlighting the seriousness of her offenses.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/i-deceived-people-i-lied-a-37-year-old-woman-pretrended-to-be-a-child-for-years-and-convinced-families-she-needed-protection-now-she-is-convicted-of-fraud/articleshow/133496640.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/i-deceived-people-i-lied-a-37-year-old-woman-pretrended-to-be-a-child-for-years-and-convinced-families-she-needed-protection-now-she-is-convicted-of-fraud/articleshow/133496640.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T11:57:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jp