="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133494804,imgsize-1001187.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Dr. Robert Parry: Ohio pediatric surgeon draws cartoons on kids’ bandages after surgery]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133494021.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-dr-robert-parry-ohio-pediatric-surgeon-draws-cartoons-on-kids-bandages-after-surgery-creating-10000-moments-of-joy/articleshow/133494021.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-dr-robert-parry-ohio-pediatric-surgeon-draws-cartoons-on-kids-bandages-after-surgery-creating-10000-moments-of-joy/articleshow/133494021.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T11:03:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133494649,imgsize-1428158.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[17-year-old Leon Wang finds 2 FDA-approved drugs that reduced Alzheimer’s-linked cell damage]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133493022.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A young student's research explored existing medicines for Alzheimer's disease protection.  He identified two drugs, nintedanib and pirfenidone, showing protective effects in cell models.  This drug repurposing approach offers a faster, less expensive research starting point.  Wang's work highlights targeting APOE4 and brain blood vessel cell changes.  His findings suggest further investigation into TGFβ pathway drugs is warranted.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/meet-leon-wang-the-17-year-old-connecticut-student-who-found-2-fda-approved-drugs-that-reduced-alzheimers-linked-damage-in-lab-gr